  "reconstruction": {
    "scope": "Specific standing Santa Cruz church and mapped monastery/cloister envelope in Coimbra: heavy western stone facade/twin faceted towers and ornate pinnacles, central pierced crest/cross, layered arched portal and tall recessed grilled window, white nave with terracotta roof, open pointed/traceried cloister arcades, upper dark windows/tile roofs, white outer ranges and original simplified central fountain. Shared stone/plaster/tile/wood/metal material graphs and original figure/foliage/spiral-shaft vocabulary; no copied narrative tile images, readable text or full church interior. Preserve Town Hall, Cafe Santa Cruz, other buildings, plaza and separate Manga monument.",
    "identityBasis": "Named standard PMTiles church building/POI35184576280912 and monastery building/POI52776561095808, correlated with ordinary facade/cloister pictures, establish the two authored controls. Named monastery point corresponds to mapped relation2962560; no exact-QID footprint attribution claimed. Anchor-8.428761,40.210945; heading0, internal local+x angle-.154600686944rad, west entrance local-x. The mapped courtyard hole is retained. Town Hall35184576280911 and Cafe Santa Cruz35184595417581 remain independent native buildings.",
    "heightBasis": "Ordinary-picture/map visualization estimates, not surveyed dimensions: approximately38.9m church length/18.5m west-front width, nave19m eaves/22m tile ridge, western stone screen24.2m, tower pinnacles29m/cross30m, center cross29m. Cloister lower arcade5m, upper glazed arcade/eaves9m, higher white outer ranges12m/terracotta ridges14m. Specific sculpture, bay subdivisions, concealed roofs and exact floor/stair levels remain approximate.",
    "terrainBasis": "Original standard6m Mapzen ground/water and all independent buildings retained. Each mapped structure has a small grade-buried local plinth; cloister courts stay native ground, entrance has short descending steps. No broad monastery/plaza slab, flattening or ground/water cutout. Coarse urban DEM does not resolve actual paved court/plaza floors or thresholds; absolute heights and approaches remain approximate.",
